抱歉 只买了两根

775
00:49:53,320 --> 00:49:57,120
Oh, no, that's no problem, I'm...I have dinner plans with my mom.
哦 不 没关系 我...我跟我妈吃

776
00:49:57,510 --> 00:49:58,620
That's not true.
不是的

777
00:49:58,650 --> 00:50:00,440
I'm sorry, I just wanted to close myself off
我怕被拒

778
00:50:00,460 --> 00:50:02,910
from the possibility of being rejected.
才装作有事的

779
00:50:04,330 --> 00:50:05,540
That's no problem.
没事

780
00:50:07,010 --> 00:50:08,610
- I'll get the lighter fluid. - Okay.
- 我去拿助燃油 - 好

781
00:50:08,630 --> 00:50:10,190
Do you wanna come inside while I look?
屋里暖和 进来坐坐？

782
00:50:10,210 --> 00:50:12,390
Uh, no, sorry. Can I wait outside?
算了 想在这儿等 行吗？

783
00:50:12,420 --> 00:50:15,930
Yeah. Don't worry about it. Um, I'll be back soon.
行 没问题 我马上给你

784
00:50:27,930 --> 00:50:29,350
This should do the trick.
这该够用

785
00:50:30,570 --> 00:50:31,730
Great, thanks.
太好了 谢谢

786
00:50:31,750 --> 00:50:36,420
And so do I just pour this on the thing I want to be on fire?
倒在要烧的东西上 就行了吧？

787
00:50:36,440 --> 00:50:39,170
On the barbecue?
烧什么 烧烤吗？

788
00:50:39,750 --> 00:50:40,760
Yes.
对

789
00:50:40,780 --> 00:50:44,420
Uh, yeah, don't put too much of it on there.
呃 嗯 别倒太多

790
00:50:45,370 --> 00:50:46,580
Okay.
好

791
00:50:46,840 --> 00:50:48,940
Do you... do you want my help?
要 要我帮忙吗？

792
00:50:48,960 --> 00:50:50,170
No.
不用

793
00:50:51,770 --> 00:50:53,100
Thank you...
谢谢你...

794
00:50:53,280 --> 00:50:54,150
Gavin.
是盖文

795
00:50:54,180 --> 00:50:58,210
Gavin. Yes. Thank you, definitely, Gavin.
对 盖文 真谢谢你 盖文

796
00:51:00,820 --> 00:51:02,530
Uh, don't you live over there?
你不是住那边吗？

797
00:51:02,550 --> 00:51:05,570
Ha! Yup, I... yup, definitely. Oops.
啥 哦 对 确实是 哈哈

798
00:51:15,360 --> 00:51:17,490
{\an1}（《乔凡尼的房间》）

799
00:51:15,360 --> 00:51:22,660
{\an9}【《乔凡尼的房间》：詹姆斯·鲍德温（美）所著小说 聚焦同性恋身份与孤独】

800
00:51:35,080 --> 00:51:36,960
Why do you have that?
从哪儿弄的？

801
00:51:37,350 --> 00:51:39,320
I got it from the neighbor.
找邻居要的

802
00:51:40,420 --> 00:51:41,800
Why?
干嘛要？

803
00:51:41,920 --> 00:51:45,450
It's definitely not, like, a good or normal train of thought.
肯定不是正常人会有的想法

804
00:51:46,010 --> 00:51:47,510
Okay.
好

805
00:51:47,980 --> 00:51:51,730
I think I was gonna light Decker's office on fire.
我本来想把德克尔办公室烧掉

806
00:51:55,950 --> 00:51:57,110
Okay...
好

807
00:51:59,200 --> 00:52:01,740
Do you still wanna do it?
你真想这么做吗

808
00:52:02,240 --> 00:52:03,600
I don't know.
没想好

809
00:52:08,050 --> 00:52:09,670
I will do it.
那我来做

810
00:52:10,740 --> 00:52:13,010
That's really nice.
你真好

811
00:52:14,920 --> 00:52:16,140
But no.
但不用

812
00:52:16,170 --> 00:52:19,780
No, seriously. If you need someone to burn his office down,
说真的 要是你想烧他办公室

813
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:23,250
but you don't wanna do it yourself, I will do it.
又不想自己去 我替你做

814
00:52:23,280 --> 00:52:26,470
No, I don't even want him to die.
不 我甚至不想咒他死

815
00:52:26,580 --> 00:52:27,970
I do.
我想

816
00:52:29,640 --> 00:52:31,800
I don't want him to die.
我不想他死

817
00:52:33,140 --> 00:52:35,600
Well, if you change your mind...
好吧 改主意了就告诉我

818
00:52:35,640 --> 00:52:36,980
Thanks.
谢谢

819
00:52:39,670 --> 00:52:42,050
Maybe we could burn something smaller,
也许一起烧点小的

820
00:52:42,070 --> 00:52:45,410
like his hair or his pens or something.
他头发或他笔之类的

821
00:52:45,730 --> 00:52:47,330
I'll think about that.
我会考虑的

822
00:52:48,660 --> 00:52:49,790
Okay.
好

823
00:52:54,080 --> 00:52:57,090
I have to make hot dogs.
哎 还得去做烤肠

824
00:52:57,120 --> 00:52:58,320
Oh, why?
为嘛？

825
00:52:58,350 --> 00:53:02,830
I told the neighbor, it's like this whole big lie. I'm stuck in a lie.
我跟邻居编了大谎 不烤心里过不去

826
00:53:02,850 --> 00:53:04,900
Okay. I will do it.
好 我来做

827
00:53:04,930 --> 00:53:06,420
I'm sorry.
对不起

828
00:53:06,450 --> 00:53:09,890
No, it's fine. I was gonna, like, kill a man, so this is much easier.
没事 我本想砍个人 相比这小菜一碟

829
00:53:09,920 --> 00:53:13,030
Do we have hot dogs?
家里有烤肠吗？

830
00:53:14,200 --> 00:53:16,010
I don't know.
不知道

831
00:54:30,600 --> 00:54:31,640
Hi.
嗨

832
00:54:38,150 --> 00:54:40,830
Okay. I'm going to get coffee.
好 我要去买咖啡

833
00:54:44,660 --> 00:54:46,790
Do you want me to pick you up?
我能抱你吗？

834
00:54:55,930 --> 00:54:58,140
Well, fuck.
哦 天呐

835
00:54:58,530 --> 00:55:01,830
This is really nice.
太美好了

836
00:55:03,390 --> 00:55:04,870
I guess um...
我想...

837
00:55:05,690 --> 00:55:08,040
Yup. I love you.
对 我爱你

838
00:55:12,680 --> 00:55:15,220
You wanna come get coffee?
愿意陪我买咖啡吗？

839
00:55:15,940 --> 00:55:17,870
Salmon.
三文鱼罐头？

840
00:55:18,440 --> 00:55:22,480
All right, you're picky, an excellent quality.
好吧 挺挑食的 有品位

841
00:55:22,530 --> 00:55:23,820
Tuna.
金枪鱼的？

842
00:55:25,940 --> 00:55:28,280
Maybe you're just smelling the can.
可能隔着罐头闻不出来

843
00:55:28,300 --> 00:55:30,280
There's tuna inside.
里面是金枪鱼

844
00:55:30,750 --> 00:55:33,030
All right, one of each.
好 各买一罐

845
00:55:49,430 --> 00:55:50,550
Hey.
嗨

846
00:55:51,560 --> 00:55:52,970
Is this all for you today?
就这些吗？

847
00:55:53,000 --> 00:55:54,700
Yes, thank you.
是的 麻烦了

848
00:55:59,490 --> 00:56:02,200
Did you bring a cat into the grocery store?
你带猫进来了吗？

849
00:56:03,170 --> 00:56:04,830
No.
没有啦

850
00:56:06,410 --> 00:56:07,550
Yes, you did.
就有

851
00:56:07,570 --> 00:56:09,530
What did you say?
信号不好 说啥？

852
00:56:09,560 --> 00:56:11,030
You're lying.
你骗人

853
00:56:11,320 --> 00:56:12,920
No, I'm not.
不 才没呢

854
00:56:19,790 --> 00:56:23,260
Here's your cat food.
您的猫粮 谢谢惠顾

855
00:56:26,130 --> 00:56:27,510
We ran out of coffee.
咖啡没了

856
00:56:27,540 --> 00:56:29,120
I got some.
我买了

857
00:56:31,130 --> 00:56:32,770
I got a cat.
我捡了只猫

858
00:56:37,530 --> 00:56:39,150
Whatever you need.
挺你啦

859
00:59:02,990 --> 00:59:09,370
{\an8}善问 恶问与自问的时光

860
00:59:06,550 --> 00:59:12,390
Thank you for being here and completing your summons.
谢谢大家来履行陪审员传召

861
00:59:12,500 --> 00:59:17,420
For those of you who haven't done this and don't know what to expect,
还没填的 不清楚流程的

862
00:59:18,250 --> 00:59:22,300
please come up and get a questionnaire.
请上前来领问卷表

863
00:59:23,220 --> 00:59:27,680
Fill it out and return it to us completed.
填好交回来

864
00:59:31,480 --> 00:59:36,060
We have little pencils if you need a little pencil.
要用笔的话 请来拿

865
00:59:36,280 --> 00:59:39,820
{\an2}（陪审员资格问卷表 姓名：安尼丝·沃德 年龄：28岁）

866
00:59:48,260 --> 00:59:57,310
{\an2}（陪审员资格问卷表 性别 女性<-->中性）

867
00:59:48,260 --> 00:59:57,310
{\an7}【自我认同性别流动 非二元 偏女性】

868
01:00:00,190 --> 01:00:04,120
The following jurors are dismissed.
以下人员免除陪审义务

869
01:00:04,140 --> 01:00:07,690
Juror one, three, five,
陪审员 1号 3号 5号

870
01:00:07,720 --> 01:00:09,960
seven, eight,
7号 8号

871
01:00:09,980 --> 01:00:12,970
30, 32,
30号 32号

872
01:00:12,990 --> 01:00:16,060
39, 25,
39号 25号

873
01:00:16,080 --> 01:00:19,430
42, 43,
42号 43号

874
01:00:19,450 --> 01:00:22,140
49, 59.
49号 59号

875
01:00:22,170 --> 01:00:24,430
You are dismissed.
你们免除义务

876
01:00:24,470 --> 01:00:27,350
Thank you. You can go.
谢谢 你们可以离庭了

877
01:00:28,620 --> 01:00:31,330
And do you think, Mrs. Fuller, based on that definition,
富勒女士 通过刚才讲解

878
01:00:31,350 --> 01:00:34,680
you understand the meaning of beyond a reasonable doubt?
您明白“排除合理怀疑”意思吗？

879
01:00:31,350 --> 01:00:34,680
{\an9}【证据使陪审员对被告有罪的怀疑不再合理】

880
01:00:34,730 --> 01:00:35,560
Yes.
明白

881
01:00:35,590 --> 01:00:37,630
That to be convinced beyond a shadow of a doubt,
要达到不怀疑的标准

882
01:00:37,650 --> 01:00:40,460
you must have been there and seen the crime with your own eyes?
在案发时非得亲眼见到吗？

883
01:00:40,490 --> 01:00:41,950
Yes. I understand.
不用 明白

884
01:00:41,970 --> 01:00:43,320
And do the rest of you feel
大家都能以

885
01:00:43,340 --> 01:00:47,690
- you can apply that idea, beyond a reasonable doubt, to this case? - Mhmm
- “排除合理怀疑”作为评判依据吗？ - 是

886
01:00:47,710 --> 01:00:50,330
How many of you have children?
有多少人是父母？

887
01:00:50,600 --> 01:00:53,530
Uh, Mr. Woguard. You have a child?
沃瓜德先生 有孩子？

888
01:00:53,560 --> 01:00:56,340
Uh, yes. Soph just turned four.
嗯 是 索菲刚满四岁

889
01:00:56,360 --> 01:00:58,260
Say you and your daughter were at the park
假设您女儿在公园

890
01:00:58,280 --> 01:00:59,760
and she's playing on the monkey bars.
玩攀爬架

891
01:00:59,790 --> 01:01:01,680
And you turned your back for a few minutes,
您有几分钟没看她

892
01:01:01,710 --> 01:01:04,640
and then she runs over to you with a broken arm.
她跑过来说胳膊伤了

893
01:01:04,660 --> 01:01:06,050
What would you think happened?
您怎么判断？

894
01:01:06,070 --> 01:01:08,350
She fell off the monkey bars and broke her arm.
她从攀爬架上掉下来摔的

895
01:01:08,370 --> 01:01:11,730
Yes, so that's an example of circumstantial evidence.
对 这就是间接证据的例子

896
01:01:11,750 --> 01:01:15,550
That's what you can reasonably infer based on the facts that you have.
根据事实可以做出的合理推断

897
01:01:15,570 --> 01:01:17,620
Does this make sense, Mr. Woguard?
沃瓜德先生 能明白吗

898
01:01:17,640 --> 01:01:18,760
Yes.
明白

899
01:01:18,880 --> 01:01:21,470
And if instead another child ran over to you
要是有其他孩子跑来告诉您

900
01:01:21,500 --> 01:01:24,890
and told you he saw her fall off the monkey bars,
说看见她怎么摔的

901
01:01:24,930 --> 01:01:28,830
that's direct testimony because someone witnessed it.
有人目击 这就是直接证词

902
01:01:28,850 --> 01:01:31,250
Does everybody understand that difference,
大家能明白

903
01:01:31,270 --> 01:01:34,840
between circumstantial evidence and direct testimony?
间接证据和直接证词的区别吗？

904
01:01:34,870 --> 01:01:36,210
Mhmm.
能

905
01:01:36,230 --> 01:01:37,670
Without direct testimony,
没有直接证词

906
01:01:37,690 --> 01:01:41,560
we cannot be positively certain a crime has been committed.
就不能肯定犯罪一定发生

907
01:01:41,590 --> 01:01:43,010
As the prosecution,
作为检方

908
01:01:43,030 --> 01:01:46,670
I must prove the defendant's guilt beyond a reasonable doubt.
我得把罪证明到排除合理怀疑

909
01:01:46,700 --> 01:01:50,020
Meaning, that there is no other reasonable explanation
即 从现有的证据中

910
01:01:50,040 --> 01:01:52,430
that can come from evidence presented.
不存在其他合理解释

911
01:01:52,460 --> 01:01:54,980
If any of you have been victims of a crime,
谁是犯罪受害者

912
01:01:55,010 --> 01:01:56,860
please raise your hand.
请举手

913
01:01:57,670 --> 01:02:00,410
Uh, Mr. Faber, what was the crime?
费伯先生 您遭遇了什么？

914
01:02:00,440 --> 01:02:02,530
Uh, I was robbed. At gunpoint.
我被抢劫了 持枪的

915
01:02:02,550 --> 01:02:03,200
Do you have any reason to believe
您认为

916
01:02:03,230 --> 01:02:05,710
that experience would make you unable to serve
那次遭遇会妨碍您

917
01:02:05,740 --> 01:02:08,230
as an impartial juror on this trial?
担任此庭公正陪审员吗？

918
01:02:08,260 --> 01:02:09,430
No.
不会

919
01:02:11,030 --> 01:02:12,470
Miss Ward.
沃德小姐

920
01:02:13,620 --> 01:02:14,450
What?
什么？

921
01:02:14,480 --> 01:02:16,500
When I asked who has been a victim of a crime,
刚问到受害者时

922
01:02:16,530 --> 01:02:17,790
did you raise your hand?
您举手了吧？

923
01:02:17,810 --> 01:02:21,800
No, I realized I shouldn't share it. So...
不是的 我不能讲这件事 就...

924
01:02:21,820 --> 01:02:25,010
You're unable to share the crime?
不能讲受害经历？

925
01:02:27,190 --> 01:02:30,710
It is frankly my worst nightmare to have to tell this whole room of strangers
这样说吧 大庭广众说出来那事儿

926
01:02:30,740 --> 01:02:32,650
about the thing that happened to me.
是我最害怕的

927
01:02:32,680 --> 01:02:33,880
So...
所以...

928
01:02:33,910 --> 01:02:37,460
that is the reasoning as to why I did not decide
所以我才把手

929
01:02:37,490 --> 01:02:39,770
to continue having my hand raised.
又放下来了

930
01:02:39,790 --> 01:02:40,970
Thank you.
见谅

931
01:02:42,650 --> 01:02:45,650
Do you think the crime would make you unable to serve
那次遭遇会妨碍您

932
01:02:45,670 --> 01:02:48,160
as an impartial juror on this case?
担任此庭公正陪审员吗？

933
01:02:48,180 --> 01:02:52,540
That is a good question, and one I've been thinking about.
问得好 我一直在想这个

934
01:02:53,430 --> 01:02:55,710
Have you come to any conclusions?
想出结论了吗？

935
01:02:55,730 --> 01:02:59,750
You know, I think I would be better not being on the jury
我觉得 退出陪审团更合适

936
01:02:59,770 --> 01:03:02,930
and instead would do better fulfilling a different civic role.
做别的事情为社会做贡献

937
01:03:02,960 --> 01:03:06,170
And what kind of civic role do you have in mind?
什么别的事情？

938
01:03:06,190 --> 01:03:10,370
So, thank you for asking. I am actually a professor,
谢谢你问 我是个教授

939
01:03:10,990 --> 01:03:13,890
part-time, hopefully soon full-time,
还没转正 期待早日实现

940
01:03:13,910 --> 01:03:15,850
which, teaching is important work.
教书很重要

941
01:03:15,870 --> 01:03:18,080
I think teaching is important.
教学是很有意义的

942
01:03:18,110 --> 01:03:22,250
Some would say that a teacher makes an ideal juror.
有人说教师是最合适的陪审员

943
01:03:22,280 --> 01:03:24,530
Absolutely not, no.
才不是呢 不

944
01:03:24,550 --> 01:03:26,360
On your questionnaire, you wrote...
你的问卷表上写着...

945
01:03:26,380 --> 01:03:27,440
Oh, no, no.
哦 别 别

946
01:03:27,470 --> 01:03:30,340
I did not know that we would be reading those aloud, so.
我没想到会被当众念出来

947
01:03:30,370 --> 01:03:32,260
"How would your friends describe you?"
“你朋友怎样形容你”

948
01:03:32,290 --> 01:03:36,000
"Smart." Crossed out, then the word "tall."
“聪明”被划掉了 改成了个“高”

949
01:03:38,970 --> 01:03:43,380
If the crime you were a victim of makes you biased, we will dismiss you.
要是那遭遇让你有偏见 就会免除你

950
01:03:45,190 --> 01:03:46,760
Can I get in trouble for telling you?
说了不会惹上事吧？

951
01:03:46,780 --> 01:03:49,110
Why would you get in trouble if you were the victim?
你是受害者 怎会有事？

952
01:03:49,140 --> 01:03:50,430
I don't know.
我不知道

953
01:03:50,450 --> 01:03:53,610
The law makes no sense in my opinion.
法律有很多不讲理的地方

954
01:03:58,450 --> 01:03:59,450
I...
那...

955
01:04:02,880 --> 01:04:06,090
I haven't said it out loud actually before.
那事我从未公开说过

956
01:04:06,120 --> 01:04:07,660
Well, that's okay.
没关系的

957
01:04:07,860 --> 01:04:09,480
Did you go to the police?
你报警了吗？

958
01:04:10,430 --> 01:04:11,520
No.
没有

959
01:04:11,720 --> 01:04:14,290
All I had was a button,
物证只有个扣子

960
01:04:14,320 --> 01:04:17,100
and I don't want him to go to jail.
我也不想见他坐牢

961
01:04:17,430 --> 01:04:18,890
Why is that?
为什么？

962
01:04:20,980 --> 01:04:23,100
He has a kid.
他有个孩子

963
01:04:28,560 --> 01:04:32,350
I want him to stop being someone who does that.
我希望给他个机会改过

964
01:04:33,160 --> 01:04:34,490
And if he went to jail,
